    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-11T04:11:11+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T04:11:11+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T17:41:11Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T17:41:11Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A ridge of high pressure to the east directs a northerly flow over South Australia. A trough and cold front about the far west will cross the state today and Monday morning. A cool southwesterly airstream will follow as a new high drifts eastwards across the Bight early this week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds west of Leigh Creek. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day. Daytime maximum temperatures 31 to 37.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds north of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-13T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-12T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h turning southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-14T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-15T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-13T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-14T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Leigh Creek, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 27.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
